WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.710
Spider-Man: Homecoming's biggest stars are
Hollywood veterans, but the film is easily

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.230
the youngest-skewing Spider-Man film ever
made.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:11.490
The story surrounds Peter Parker and a crowd
of fresh-faced characters that includes Michelle,

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.019
played by 20-year-old Zendaya Coleman, an
actress and singer known professionally as

00:00:15.019 --> 00:00:16.160
just "Zendaya."

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.470
If you feel like you've seen Zendaya before,
you're probably right—she's been pretty

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:23.320
busy over the last few years, earning increasingly
higher-profile roles.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.720
So now's the perfect time to familiarize yourself
with the former Disney star who's turning

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.890
heads in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.570
​Shake It Up!

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:35.629
If you know Zendaya from anywhere, it's either
those "X Out" skin care commercials, or the

00:00:35.629 --> 00:00:40.410
musical sitcom Shake It Up! that ran from
2010 to 2013 on the Disney Channel.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:45.399
In her breakout role as Rocky Blue, she starred
alongside Bella Thorne's CeCe Jones as background

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:47.329
dancers on a local dance series.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:51.460
A big hit for the channel, Shake It Up! also
spawned several music videos, turning Zendaya

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:55.800
and Thorne into household names — at least
in households including pre-teen girls with

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.120
an affinity for Disney ...

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.120
Frenemies

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:04.210
Along with starring in Shake It Up!, Zendaya
and Thorne also anchored the 2012 Disney Channel

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:08.920
made-for-TV movie Frenemies, comprised of
three intertwined stories about the misadventures

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.230
of teens who are feuding with everyone from
their best pal to their pet dog.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:17.110
Viewed by more than four million people upon
its premiere, the film proved there was plenty

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.260
of demand for Zendaya outside her hit series.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.670
Her debut album

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:25.909
The same year Shake It Up! ended its run,
Zendaya stepped out as a solo artist, releasing

00:01:25.909 --> 00:01:30.560
her self-titled debut LP through Disney's
music imprint, Hollywood Records.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.860
Although the album wasn't a blockbuster hit,
it performed respectably, peaking at No. 51

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:39.899
on Billboard and earning critical praise from
outlets like AllMusic, who deemed it a "streamlined,

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.520
self-assured first effort."

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.090
You may have caught Zendaya promoting the
record during a Today Show appearance in 2013,

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.920
performing her Top 40 hit "Replay" …

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.240
Zapped

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:03.570
Zendaya got a chance to headline her own Disney
Channel original film in 2014 with Zapped,

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:07.650
which tells the story of a teen who realizes
her phone is suddenly able to control all

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:08.940
the boys at her school.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:13.360
Zaniness ensues, of course, but Zendaya's
character eventually learns a valuable lesson

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.800
about how to treat people.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.470
The broadcast gave the budding star another
hit for the channel: it was viewed by nearly

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:22.800
six million people following its premiere,
ending up as the most-watched cable broadcast

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.140
of the night.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.510
Bad Blood

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:30.720
She's made plenty of her own music videos
as a Disney starlet, but in 2015, Zendaya

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.190
made a high-profile cameo for another artist:
Taylor Swift.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:38.130
In Swift's "Bad Blood" video, Zendaya plays
a character called Cut Throat, and if you're

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:42.660
among the millions who saw the star-studded
clip in 2015, it might be one reason you thought

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.760
she looked familiar in Spider-Man: Homecoming.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.760
Black-ish

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:53.280
In 2015, Zendaya appeared in ABC's hit dramedy
series Black-ish as a guest star in the episode

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.280
"Daddy's Day."

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.910
Her character Resheida complicates an emotional
tug-of-war between Dre and his daughter Zoey.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:02.450
Though she was obviously a known commodity
thanks to her Disney Channel tenure, this

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:06.700
Black-ish role put the young star in front
of a whole new group of potential fans outside

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:07.890
the Disney bubble.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:08.890
​K.C.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:09.980
Undercover

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.900
After sharing the spotlight in Shake It Up,
Zendaya took center stage in her own Disney

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.340
Channel sitcom with K.C.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.110
Undercover, which premiered in 2015.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.470
Zendaya plays genius high school student K.C.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:24.090
Cooper, who learns her parents are actually
spies — and they want to recruit her.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.700
"For the last time: who are you?"

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:27.700
"I'll never talk!"

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:29.880
"My name is K.C.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.570
Cooper and I'm a 16-year-old government spy!"

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:35.220
And although it might have seemed like a bit
of a step back to return to her cable roots

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:39.410
just as her big-screen career was poised to
take off, she definitely had some compelling

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.410
reasons.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:44.230
As Zendaya told Marie Claire, "A big reason
why I wanted to come back to Disney is because

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.540
I saw a lack of diversity on the channel.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.920
To see a black family, to see a young girl
with these adorable Afro puffs…little things

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.120
like that are so important."

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.120
All Night

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:59.790
Zendaya's good luck streak with music video
cameo appearances continued in 2016, when

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.670
she was asked to film a part for Beyoncé's
"All Night."

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:06.480
Aside from the thrill of working with a global
superstar she claimed she'd been "obsessed

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.620
with" since birth, Zendaya told People she
felt like she got to be "a part of music history"

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:15.140
on the shoot, which helped round out the visual
album Beyoncé crafted for her acclaimed Lemonade

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.140
LP.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:20.230
As of now, it's been watched more than 47
million times—an impressive number even

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:24.900
when you put it alongside a worldwide box-office
smash like Spider-Man: Homecoming.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:25.900
Thanks for watching!

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.190
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:30.510
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

